<title>USA: TransAmerica repurchased 3.0 mln shares.</title>
<headline>TransAmerica repurchased 3.0 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transamerica Corp said Friday it has repurchased 3 million shares of its common stock.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it bought the shares from two investment banks for about $273 million based on an average price of $91.11 a share.</p>
<p>To complete the transaction, the investment banks are borrowing Transamerica common shares and will buy replacement shares on the open market.</p>
<p>The company said it paid for the shares with a portion of the proceeds from the sale of its consumer finance unit to Household International, which was completed June 23.</p>
<p>Transamerica has about 63.3 million shares outstanding after the repurchase.</p>
<p>Its common shares closed Friday at 94-1/8, up 5/8.</p>
